{
  "slug": "2026-taiwan-creative-expo",
  "name": "2026 臺灣文博會 品牌商展",
  "nameEn": "Creative Expo Taiwan 2026 — Creative Brands",
  "summary": "臺灣規模最大的文化品牌年度展會，設計、工藝、選物與生活風格品牌齊聚，一次看盡當代臺灣品牌的樣貌。",
  "summaryEn": "Taiwan's largest annual cultural-brand showcase — design, craft, select goods and lifestyle brands together in one place.",
  "description": "2026 臺灣文博會由文化部主辦，國立臺灣工藝研究發展中心與文化內容策進院共同合辦，是台灣規模最大的文化創意內容展示、產業交流與市場媒合平台。今年的年度主題是「第零位元 Bit Zero」，談的是在演算法可以無限複製內容的時代裡，什麼才是無法被取代的原創。\n\n展會分成兩個部分：文化策展在空總臺灣當代文化實驗場的古蹟大樓，品牌商展則在臺北南港展覽館一館。這一頁整理的是品牌商展，逾 870 個品牌、1,200 個攤位，分為 IP 授權展區、文創品牌展區與新銳品牌展區。2025 年的文博會吸引 65 萬人次入場，專業買家超過 2.8 萬人次。\n\n三個展區裡，攤位都是付費租用，主辦單位做的是資格審查而非策展篩選；唯一的例外是新銳品牌展區，該區 100 個攤位由評審依市場力、創新力與設計力評選產生。本站收錄的 123 個品牌中，121 個在文創品牌與新銳品牌展區，只有 2 個在 IP 授權展區。",
  "descriptionEn": "Creative Expo Taiwan 2026 is organized by the Ministry of Culture with the National Taiwan Craft Research and Development Center and TAICCA, and describes itself as Taiwan's leading platform for showcasing cultural and creative content, industry exchange, and market matchmaking. This year's theme is 「Bit Zero」, asking what counts as irreplaceable originality in an age when algorithms can replicate content without limit.\n\nThe expo runs in two parts: the curated cultural exhibition at the C-LAB heritage building, and the brand trade show at Taipei Nangang Exhibition Center, Hall 1. This page covers the trade show: over 870 brands across more than 1,200 booths, split into IP Licensing, Cultural & Creative Brands, and Start-ups. The 2025 edition drew 650,000 visitors and more than 28,000 professional attendees.\n\nBooths in all three zones are paid rentals and the organizer screens for eligibility rather than curating; the one exception is the Start-ups zone, where all 100 booths are awarded by a jury scoring market strength, innovation, and design. Of the 123 directory brands exhibiting, 121 are in the two brand zones and only 2 are in IP Licensing.",
  "startsOn": "2026-08-06",
  "endsOn": "2026-08-12",
